---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lessons = [
  {
    number: 49,
    title: "Libraries in BASIC",
    description: "Build a reusable toolkit of drawing and sound routines",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 50,
    title: "Title Screens",
    description: "Animate attract-mode banners while waiting for start",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 51,
    title: "Menus & Options",
    description: "Navigate choices with keyboard or joystick dispatch",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 52,
    title: "Multiple Levels",
    description: "Load stages from structured DATA blocks on demand",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 53,
    title: "Cutscenes in BASIC",
    description: "Script story beats with timed, skippable dialogue",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 54,
    title: "Debugging Retro-Style",
    description: "Trace variables, pause loops, and build a debug HUD",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 55,
    title: "Optimising for Speed",
    description: "Measure and precompute to keep BASIC loops responsive",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 56,
    title: "Galactic Miner",
    description: "Mini-game weaving states, AI, cutscenes, and scores",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 57,
    title: "Making It Feel Right",
    description: "Tune controls with fixed steps, easing, and trace HUDs",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 58,
    title: "Squeezing Speed",
    description: "Profile hotspots, cache data, and unroll loops for speed",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 59,
    title: "When BASIC Breaks",
    description: "Handle DATA, memory, and input failures gracefully",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 60,
    title: "Under the Skin",
    description: "Inspect BASIC pointers, screen RAM, and colour memory",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 61,
    title: "POKE the Future",
    description: "Install machine code helpers and call them with SYS",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 62,
    title: "Looking Below",
    description: "Compare BASIC routines with their assembly equivalents",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 63,
    title: "The Threshold",
    description: "Monitor frame budgets and decide what to port next",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 64,
    title: "Retrospective: The Journey So Far",
    description: "Celebrate the course and prepare for assembly programming",
    status: "available"
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Tier 4: Polish & Performance - Phase 0 - Commodore 64"
  description="Complete your BASIC journey: build libraries, create menus and cutscenes, optimize performance, and bridge to machine code. Prepare for 6502 assembly. Coming soon."
>
  <style>
    .course-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4a4dff 0%, #7c70da 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .course-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    }

    .course-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .course-description {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      opacity: 0.95;
    }

    .course-stats {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .stat-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .stat-value {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .stat-label {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      opacity: 0.9;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .content-container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .intro-section {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #4a4dff;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .intro-section h2 {
      color: #4a4dff;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .intro-section p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .intro-section ul {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      padding-left: var(--space-6);
    }

    .intro-section li {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .lessons-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .lesson-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .lesson-card:hover {
      border-color: #4a4dff;
      transform: translateX(4px);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(74, 77, 255, 0.1);
    }

    .lesson-number {
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4a4dff 0%, #7c70da 100%);
      color: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .lesson-content {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .lesson-title {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .lesson-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .lesson-status {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      border-radius: 9999px;
      background: rgba(74, 77, 255, 0.1);
      color: #4a4dff;
    }

    .start-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4a4dff 0%, #7c70da 100%);
      color: white;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .start-button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(74, 77, 255, 0.3);
    }

    .wow-box {
      background: var(--color-bg);
      border-left: 4px solid #4a4dff;
      padding: var(--space-4);
      margin: var(--space-6) 0;
      border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
    }

    .wow-box strong {
      color: #4a4dff;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .back-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      text-decoration: none;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    }

    .back-link:hover {
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .lesson-card {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .lesson-number {
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .lesson-status {
        justify-self: center;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Course Hero -->
  <section class="course-hero">
    <h1 class="course-title">TIER 4: POLISH & PERFORMANCE</h1>
    <p class="course-subtitle">Phase 0 - BASIC Gateway</p>

    <p class="course-description">
      Complete your BASIC mastery with professional polish, optimization, and understanding BASIC's limits. These final 16 lessons teach libraries, menus, cutscenes, debugging, performance tuning, and bridging to assembly. Graduate ready for pure machine code.
    </p>

    <div class="course-stats">
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">16</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Lessons</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">15–20</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Minutes Each</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">1</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Complete Game</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Course Introduction -->
  <div class="content-container">
    <a href="/commodore-64/phase-0" class="back-link">
      ← Back to Phase 0
    </a>

    <section class="intro-section">
      <h2>What You'll Learn This Tier</h2>

      <p>
        Tier 4 brings professional polish and prepares you for assembly programming. You'll learn:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Code libraries</strong> - Reusable routines for drawing, sound, and utilities</li>
        <li><strong>Title screens & menus</strong> - Attract modes, navigation, and options</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-level systems</strong> - Stage progression with data-driven design</li>
        <li><strong>Narrative cutscenes</strong> - Timed, skippable story beats</li>
        <li><strong>Debugging techniques</strong> - Variable tracing, pause loops, debug HUDs</li>
        <li><strong>Performance optimization</strong> - Profiling hotspots, caching, loop unrolling</li>
        <li><strong>Error handling</strong> - Graceful failures for DATA, memory, input</li>
        <li><strong>Memory inspection</strong> - Understanding BASIC pointers and RAM layout</li>
        <li><strong>Machine code integration</strong> - Installing and calling assembly helpers with SYS</li>
        <li><strong>Frame budgets</strong> - Monitoring performance limits and deciding what to port</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="wow-box">
        <strong>Tier 4 Goal:</strong> Build "Galactic Miner" (complete game with menus, cutscenes, multiple levels) and understand BASIC's performance boundaries. Graduate ready to tackle assembly programming in Phase 1.
      </div>

      <p>
        <strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Complete Tiers 1-3 (lessons 1-48). You'll build on all prior techniques and push BASIC to its limits.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Lessons List -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Lessons</h2>

      <div class="lessons-grid">
        {lessons.map(lesson => (
          <a href={`/commodore-64/phase-0/tier-4/lesson-${String(lesson.number).padStart(3, '0')}`}
             class="lesson-card">
            <div class="lesson-number">{lesson.number}</div>
            <div class="lesson-content">
              <h3 class="lesson-title">{lesson.title}</h3>
              <p class="lesson-description">{lesson.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-status">Start →</div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <section style="text-align: center; margin: var(--space-16) 0;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Ready to Polish?</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        You've built complete games. Now let's add professional polish, optimize performance,
        and understand BASIC's limits before moving to pure assembly!
      </p>
      <a href="/commodore-64/phase-0/tier-4/lesson-049" class="start-button">
        Start Lesson 49: Libraries in BASIC
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
